{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgnkYeXruPoGnsU3D1rz8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The original file was a bare `<svg>` root element with nothing inside it, so there was no artwork to improve. I rewrote it as a complete, valid skeleton:\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"\n     width=\"100\" height=\"100\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"\n     role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"svg-title svg-desc\">\n  <title id=\"svg-title\">Untitled</title>\n  <desc id=\"svg-desc\">Empty 100 by 100 canvas. Add shapes inside this element.</desc>\n</svg>\n```\n\nWhat changed and why:\n\n- **Explicit size and viewBox.** Without them, browsers render an undefined 300 by 150 box and scaling behaves unpredictably. Now the image has a fixed coordinate system and scales cleanly.\n- **Accessibility metadata.** The role attribute plus linked title and description give screen readers a name for the image instead of silence.\n- **XML declaration.** Standalone SVG files benefit from a declared encoding, and some tools require it.\n\nOne thing I could not do: the `xmllint` well-formedness check was blocked by the permission system in this session. I verified the markup by hand instead. The tags are balanced, attributes are quoted, and there is a single namespaced root, so it should parse without errors.\n\nThe file still renders as a blank canvas because it had no content to begin with. If you want an actual drawing, tell me what it should show and I'll add the shapes inside this structure."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":8916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":563},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnos